\section{The [[submissions view]] subcommand and its options}

Here we provide a subcommand [[submissions view]] which deals with an individual 
submission.
<<submission command description>>=
Prints data about matching submissions, including submission and grading time, 
and any text-based attachments.

By default, placeholder rows without student work or instructor feedback are
hidden. Pass [[--include-null-submissions]] to inspect those rows as well.

We also need the corresponding function.
For now, we only print the most relevant data of a submission.
<<functions>>=
def submissions_view_command(config, canvas, args):
  <<enable history when diff is requested>>
  
  submission_list = filter_view_submissions(
    process_submission_options(canvas, args),
    include_null_submissions=args.include_null_submissions)
  if not submission_list:
    raise canvaslms.cli.EmptyListError(
      "No submissions found matching the criteria")

  <<get and print the submission data>>
@

The shared selection helper intentionally leaves null submissions in place,
because [[submissions list]] and [[submissions grade]] use them to reason about
absence. For the viewing commands that same data is mostly noise: rendering a
record with neither student work nor instructor feedback only repeats metadata.
We therefore filter null submissions after the shared selection step, leaving
the other commands untouched.

A submission stops being null as soon as Canvas records either work or
feedback. That includes actual submission artefacts such as timestamps,
text bodies, quiz answers, and attachments, but also instructor feedback such
as comments, rubric assessments, and manually recorded grades.
History needs one extra check. Canvas may attach a metadata-only [[Version 0]]
to an otherwise empty record, so a non-empty [[submission_history]] is not
enough on its own. We inspect each historical version for the same signals that
make the current submission meaningful.
Canvas's [[preview_url]] does not count on its own: it is a link to Canvas's
preview page, not evidence that the student uploaded work or entered a text
submission.
<<constants>>=
NON_NULL_SUBMISSION_WORKFLOW_STATES = {
  "submitted",
  "graded",
  "pending_review",
}
@

<<functions>>=
def filter_view_submissions(submission_list,
                            include_null_submissions=False):
  """Return the submissions that the view commands should render."""
  submission_list = list(submission_list)
  if include_null_submissions:
    return submission_list

  return [
    submission for submission in submission_list
    if not is_null_submission(submission)
  ]

def is_meaningful_submission(submission):
  """Return True when ``submission`` contains work or feedback."""
  submission = canvaslms.cli.utils.ensure_submission_attrs(submission)
  return (
    bool(submission.submitted_at) or
    submission.workflow_state in NON_NULL_SUBMISSION_WORKFLOW_STATES or
    bool(submission.body) or
    bool(submission.submission_data) or
    bool(submission.attachments) or
    bool(submission.submission_comments) or
    bool(submission.rubric_assessment) or
    submission.grade not in (None, "")
  )

def has_meaningful_submission_history(submission):
  """Return True when history contains work or feedback."""
  submission = canvaslms.cli.utils.ensure_submission_attrs(submission)
  if not submission.submission_history:
    return False

  for prev_submission in submission.submission_history:
    prev_submission = canvasapi.submission.Submission(
      submission._requester, prev_submission)
    if is_meaningful_submission(prev_submission):
      return True

  return False

def is_null_submission(submission):
  """Return True when ``submission`` is only placeholder metadata."""
  return not (
    is_meaningful_submission(submission) or
    has_meaningful_submission_history(submission)
  )
@

\subsection{Verifying null-submission filtering}

The view commands suppress placeholder rows by default, but they must still
show records that carry either actual work or instructor feedback. These tests
fix the boundary between a truly empty placeholder, including Canvas's
metadata-only history entries, and a record that already contains comments,
rubric feedback, grades, or historical work.

<<test functions>>=
def make_submission(**attrs):
    """Build a submission mock with the attrs used by view filtering."""
    submission = Mock(spec=[
        "_requester",
        "submitted_at",
        "workflow_state",
        "body",
        "submission_data",
        "attachments",
        "submission_history",
        "preview_url",
        "submission_comments",
        "rubric_assessment",
        "grade",
    ])
    submission._requester = Mock()
    submission.submitted_at = None
    submission.workflow_state = "unsubmitted"
    submission.body = None
    submission.submission_data = None
    submission.attachments = []
    submission.submission_history = []
    submission.preview_url = None
    submission.submission_comments = []
    submission.rubric_assessment = None
    submission.grade = None

    for name, value in attrs.items():
        setattr(submission, name, value)

    return submission


class TestNullSubmissions:
    """Test detection of placeholder submissions for view."""

    @pytest.mark.parametrize(
        ("attrs", "expected"),
        [
            ({}, True),
            ({"submitted_at": "2024-01-01T10:00:00Z"}, False),
            ({"workflow_state": "submitted"}, False),
            ({"preview_url": "https://canvas.example/submissions/1?preview=1"},
             True),
            ({"submission_history": [{}]}, True),
            ({"submission_history": [{"body": "answer"}]}, False),
