\subsection{Verifying local ungraded filtering}

The cache fix depends on two details: the ungraded predicate must stay
consistent across commands, and [[list_ungraded_submissions()]] must fetch the
full submission set instead of delegating the filter to Canvas.

<<test functions>>=
class TestListUngradedSubmissions:
    """Test local ungraded submission filtering."""

    @pytest.mark.parametrize(
        ("submitted_at", "graded_at", "matches_current", "expected"),
        [
            ("2024-01-01T10:00:00Z", None, None, True),
            ("2024-01-01T10:00:00Z", "2024-01-01T12:00:00Z", False, True),
            ("2024-01-01T10:00:00Z", "2024-01-01T12:00:00Z", True, False),
            (None, None, None, False),
        ],
    )
    def test_uses_shared_ungraded_predicate(
        self, submitted_at, graded_at, matches_current, expected
    ):
        """Ungraded means either never graded or changed after grading."""
        submission = Mock(spec=[
            "submitted_at",
            "graded_at",
            "grade_matches_current_submission",
        ])
        submission.submitted_at = submitted_at
        submission.graded_at = graded_at
        submission.grade_matches_current_submission = matches_current

        assert is_ungraded(submission) is expected

    def test_fetches_full_collection_without_bucket(self):
        """Ungraded listing should filter locally after a plain fetch."""
        assignment = Mock()

        graded = Mock(spec=[
            "submitted_at",
            "graded_at",
            "grade_matches_current_submission",
        ])
        graded.submitted_at = "2024-01-01T10:00:00Z"
        graded.graded_at = "2024-01-01T12:00:00Z"
        graded.grade_matches_current_submission = True

        never_graded = Mock(spec=[
            "submitted_at",
            "graded_at",
            "grade_matches_current_submission",
        ])
        never_graded.submitted_at = "2024-01-01T10:05:00Z"
        never_graded.graded_at = None
        never_graded.grade_matches_current_submission = None

        resubmitted = Mock(spec=[
            "submitted_at",
            "graded_at",
            "grade_matches_current_submission",
        ])
        resubmitted.submitted_at = "2024-01-01T10:10:00Z"
        resubmitted.graded_at = "2024-01-01T12:10:00Z"
        resubmitted.grade_matches_current_submission = False

        assignment.get_submissions.return_value = [
            graded,
            never_graded,
            resubmitted,
        ]

        result = list(list_ungraded_submissions(
            [assignment],
            include=["submission_comments"],
            check_bulk_refresh=True,
        ))

        assignment.get_submissions.assert_called_once_with(
            include=["submission_comments"],
            check_bulk_refresh=True,
            student_ids=None,
        )
        assert result == [never_graded, resubmitted]
        assert never_graded.assignment is assignment
        assert resubmitted.assignment is assignment
@


\section{Filtering a list of submissions}

We provide the function [[filter_submissions]] which filters out a subset of 
submissions from a list.

For each submission we check if it's user is in the desired user set.
(Note that since the list~[[user_list]], might contain duplicates, so we turn 
it into a set first.)
Once we've found the user, we don't need to search further, so we can break 
after the yield.
<<functions>>=
def filter_submissions(submission_list, user_list):
  user_list = set(user_list)

  for submission in submission_list:
    for user in user_list:
      if submission.user_id == user.id:
        submission.user = user
        yield submission
        break
@


\section{Printing a submission}

We provide two functions to print a submission.
One to print a short summary (row in CSV data) and one to print the submission 
data for rendering.
The first is to get an overview of all submissions, the latter to look into the 
details of only one submission.

We'll format the submission in short format.
The most useful data is the identifier, the grade and the date of grading.
<<functions>>=
def format_submission_short(submission):
  return [
    submission.assignment.course.course_code,
    submission.assignment.name,
    submission.user.name,
    submission.grade,
    canvaslms.cli.utils.format_local_time(submission.submitted_at),
    canvaslms.cli.utils.format_local_time(submission.graded_at)
  ]
@

